# 19. Do Not Break Existing Functionality

This is mandatory.

Do not change:

- Existing PLP layout.
- Product cards.
- Product links.
- Sorting.
- Pagination.
- Existing filters.
- Category selection.
- Search behavior.
- Wishlist behavior.
- Cart behavior.
- Magento integration unrelated to price filtering.
- Existing mobile navigation.
- Existing responsive layout.

Only change code required for the price filter.

If an existing implementation is fragile, make the smallest safe refactor necessary and explain why.

---

# 20. No Fallback / Dummy Data

Do NOT implement:

```ts
const maxPrice = apiMaxPrice || 900000;
```

if the requirement is to use real catalog data.

Do NOT implement:

```ts
const products = apiProducts || dummyProducts;
```

Do NOT invent prices.

If required API data is missing:

- Handle the missing/null state according to existing project conventions.
- Hide/disable the relevant UI where appropriate.
- Do not fabricate data.

